  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef matrix_addition(a: list, b: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute elementwise addition of two identically shaped 2D matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nCompute elementwise addition of two identically shaped 2D matrices.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef matrix_addition(a: list, b: list) -> list:\n    return np.round(np.array(a, dtype=float) + np.array(b, dtype=float), 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
